module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_cast_to_string_of_a_nominal_value_renders_host_debug_text

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_cast_to_string_of_a_nominal_value_renders_host_debug_text: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_cast_to_string_of_a_nominal_value_renders_host_debug_text" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the seed checker deciding every explicit `as` crossing from the declared conversion routes alone, SUFFICIENT FOR v1.compiler.infer validate_cast to refuse, located, any cast whose source is a nominal product or coproduct and whose target has no declared route (as `true as Int` already refuses), and for the Value::Variant | Value::Record arm of v1_interpreter eval_cast's String target to be unreachable and deleted; the whole-corpus differential lists the newly refused sites, each fixed forward with its declared conversion" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: `e as String` where `e` is a nominal product (a record) or coproduct is ACCEPTED with no declared conversion, and at runtime yields the host's debug rendering of the value. HARM: a plausible but wrong string reaches an output or a request (DESIGN section 5, fabricated plausible output); every Int -> record-carrier migration silently turns an existing `as String` over the old Int into this defect, because the cast keeps compiling.",
    "SPECIMEN (found live, gunbc#14732, 2026-10-22): gunbc.superseded_run_starvation_census refresh_pair had `run_id: pair.live_head_run as String`; when the field became the carrier GitHubWorkflowRunId { value: Int } the line kept compiling, a GitHub ListJobs request would have carried `GitHubWorkflowRunId { value: 35447067113 }` as its run id, and its witness stayed green. The declared conversion github_workflow_run_id_wire_text renders `35447067113`.",
    "MEASURED ON MAIN (9cad1c9e6c2, 2026-10-22; one remote dispatch building the `gunbc` binary from v1-compiler and running the probes on the same runner; probes `type P { value: Int }`, `type Q { a: Int, b: String }`, `type C = Red | Green { n: Int }`, `fn main` returning the cast). `p as String` -> compiles, runs, `P { value: 35447067113 }`. `q as String` -> `Q { a: 1, b: x }`. coproduct `Red as String` -> `Red`, `Green { n: 7 } as String` -> `Green { n: 7 }`. `concat(\"id=\", p)` -> `id=P { value: 35447067113 }` (the same rendering without a cast; concat is a second route to the same text). GRAIN: `p as Int` and a coproduct `as Int` are ACCEPTED by the checker and refused at runtime (`TypeError cannot cast P (runtime carrier Record) to Int`), the case the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses owns; `List<Int> as String` is likewise accepted and refused at runtime (`cannot cast List to String`); `Bool as Int` is REFUSED at compile time (`invalid cast: Bool as Int`). So the defect is specific to the String target over a Record or Variant carrier, where the evaluator ACCEPTS rather than refuses.",
    "CHAIN (DESIGN section 6b). Link a, the declared-type authority: std.coercion dag_cast_rules rosters only Int, Float and Bool, and a record or coproduct has no route to String declared anywhere. Link b, the checker: v1.compiler.infer validate_cast returns none (admits) whenever either side is outside the dag_cast_rules domain (is_dag_cast_domain_type), so an undeclared crossing is ABSTAINED on, not refused; the abstention is the seed's own recorded residue (a cast outside the domain is 'decided by eval alone'). Link c, the evaluator: v1_interpreter eval_cast, target String, renders `Value::Variant { .. } | Value::Record { .. }` through the host Display (`format!(\"{}\", val)`), commented as 'corpus wire/debug casts for structured values'. EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY: link b. DESIGN section 4 makes coercion the implicit-safe subset of DECLARED conversions and says target realization never decides whether a conversion is legal; validate_cast turns 'no declared route' into 'legal' by abstaining, and eval_cast then supplies a route (host debug text) that no declaration owns, so the evaluator's cast table is deciding legality. Repairing eval_cast alone would leave the checker blessing a cast the evaluator refuses (the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses), so the repair belongs at validate_cast with eval_cast's arm derived from the same rows.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, home search: the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses owns checker-accepts/evaluator-refuses and names this domain as its RESIDUE, but its harm is a runtime crash; here the evaluator accepts and fabricates. identity_cast_compares_type_spellings and as_cast_has_no_lowered_form (v2 lowering) are different relations. two_admission_authorities_keyed_on_different_relations is the v1/v2 roster fork. annotated_let_judged_by_the_cast_relation_not_the_inhabitance_relation and declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel are declared-type walls, not explicit casts. Filed as its own row because the harm (silent wrong text) and the rung (below the ladder, not a located runtime error) differ from every candidate; it names the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses as the sibling that owns the refusing half.",
    "CENSUS, SOUND ONLY AS CANDIDATES: no instrument reads the typed program for this. The seed has no pass listing casts by resolved source type, so the census is a text scan of dag/ and src/v2/ (about 19,000 ` as String` occurrences, 2,400 files, almost all NonEmptyStr or String refinements) filtered by a declared-parameter-type heuristic, then each hit verified by reading. The heuristic misses operands whose type comes from a let, a pattern or a field chain off a binding, and it over-reports bindings shadowed by a pattern; so the list is a LOWER BOUND. The typed census is the Phase 2 whole-corpus differential once validate_cast refuses. VERIFIED WRONG, debug text reaches a produced value: gunbc.source_integration_landing_spine landing_native_refusal `refusal_receipt: refusal.receipt as String` (receipt is a ContentHash coproduct, the text lands in NativeScmRefusal.refusal_receipt). VERIFIED DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_verification_receipt `expected.criteria_digest as String` and `found.criteria_digest as String` (Fnv1a64Structural record, rendered into the VerificationSubjectDiffers expected/found fields of a refusal message). NOT PRODUCTS, ruled out by reading: workspace_microvm_access host_key (NonEmptyStr), nccl NcclChannelUnreadableLines causes (NonEmptyStr), custody and workspace_checkpoint payload bindings (String), the Nat sites (Nat is grounded onto Int).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
